invariant: INV-16
file: src/mldsa_sign_pack.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh keccak
reason: ExpandMask squeezes y's stream under 0 in place of the session's
  value, so a signer whose caller stated CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3 hashes
  that part of each round on sha3.c. Every byte stays right, so no vector
  notices, and the signature only loses speed. bin/mldsa_runtime_test
  counts each SHAKE call on each path under every ch_cfg.cpu value and
  requires all of them on the instructions' path under the bit. Only an
  arm64 object that clang compiled has that path, so the script builds the
  binary with clang for arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64.

--- old
    mld_absorb(cpu, &h, rho2, 64);
    mld_absorb(cpu, &h, index, sizeof index);
    mld_squeeze(cpu, &h, stream, sizeof stream);
--- new
    mld_absorb(cpu, &h, rho2, 64);
    mld_absorb(cpu, &h, index, sizeof index);
    mld_squeeze(0, &h, stream, sizeof stream);
